course: dictionary
lesson: 13959
title: Lightless
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Lightless is made of two parts: light and -less. The ending -less means without, so lightless means without light. «The cave was lightless, so we switched on our torch.» The torch was needed because there was no light at all.
explain: Lightless is stronger than dark. A dark room may have a little light coming under the door, but a lightless place has none, not even a glimmer. «Far down in the ocean, the water is lightless.»
explain: Writers use lightless to make a place feel mysterious or scary. Check the meaning by swapping in a word: «The water is dark» still makes sense, and lightless adds the idea of total darkness.
fact: Lightless is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a lightless cave.
fact: Lightless means with no light at all; completely dark.
fact: The ending -less means without, as in hopeless (without hope) and careless (without care).
fact: Animals living in lightless places may be blind or make their own light.
fact: Lightless is a literary word, found in stories and science books.
exercise: «The cave was lightless, so we switched on our torch.» What does lightless mean? | Very cold and wet | Very quiet | *With no light at all | Full of bright, shining stars
exercise: The root word is light. What does the ending -less mean? | Very much | *Without | Again | Under
exercise: Which word means the same as lightless? | Sunny | Noisy | Shiny | *Completely dark
test: «Deep under the sea, the water is lightless.» Why might a writer choose lightless here? | It means the water is warm | It shows the sea is bright and sunny | It means the sea is shallow | *It tells the reader the place has no light at all
test: Why might animals that live in lightless caves be blind? | They ate too many carrots | They are too busy to look | They are scared of the sun | *Living where there is no light, they may lose their sight
exam: «The lightless room felt scary.» What does lightless mean? | *Completely dark | Full of toys | Bright and noisy | Warm and cosy
